        "updatedAt": "2022-01-02T14:24:09Z"
    },
    "closed": true,
    "closedAt": "2024-12-19T11:00:41Z",
    "comment_count": 1,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                "login": "echasnovski",
                "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Do you have any plans to make mini.pick match items in any order, like fzf-lua does?\r\n\r\nIn theory this is possible via some additional flag on how [\"grouped fuzzy\"](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/7ebfab26d77a4b9b05aaae565907e7fa4b2ee154/doc/mini-pick.txt#L892-L893) mode operates. Now it indeed [matches in order](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/7ebfab26d77a4b9b05aaae565907e7fa4b2ee154/doc/mini-pick.txt#L868-L870) which is aligned with how overall fuzzy matching is done.\r\n\r\nIn practice, I don't think this is a good idea to begin with. All default matching in 'mini.pick' is done in query order and is a big factor when it comes to optimizing matching speed. So I don't think this will be implemented as built-in.\r\n\r\nMy best suggestion would be to implement this manually as [default `config.source.match`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/7ebfab26d77a4b9b05aaae565907e7fa4b2ee154/doc/mini-pick.txt#L753) (it should follow [this specification](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/7ebfab26d77a4b9b05aaae565907e7fa4b2ee154/doc/mini-pick.txt#L308)).",
            "bodyHTML": "<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Do you have any plans to make mini.pick match items in any order, like fzf-lua does?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">In theory this is possible via some additional flag on how <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/7ebfab26d77a4b9b05aaae565907e7fa4b2ee154/doc/mini-pick.txt#L892-L893\">\"grouped fuzzy\"</a> mode operates. Now it indeed <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/7ebfab26d77a4b9b05aaae565907e7fa4b2ee154/doc/mini-pick.txt#L868-L870\">matches in order</a> which is aligned with how overall fuzzy matching is done.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">In practice, I don't think this is a good idea to begin with. All default matching in 'mini.pick' is done in query order and is a big factor when it comes to optimizing matching speed. So I don't think this will be implemented as built-in.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">My best suggestion would be to implement this manually as <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/7ebfab26d77a4b9b05aaae565907e7fa4b2ee154/doc/mini-pick.txt#L753\">default <code class=\"notranslate\">config.source.match</code></a> (it should follow <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/7ebfab26d77a4b9b05aaae565907e7fa4b2ee154/doc/mini-pick.txt#L308\">this specification</a>).</p>",
            "bodyText": "Do you have any plans to make mini.pick match items in any order, like fzf-lua does?\n\nIn theory this is possible via some additional flag on how \"grouped fuzzy\" mode operates. Now it indeed matches in order which is aligned with how overall fuzzy matching is done.\nIn practice, I don't think this is a good idea to begin with. All default matching in 'mini.pick' is done in query order and is a big factor when it comes to optimizing matching speed. So I don't think this will be implemented as built-in.\nMy best suggestion would be to implement this manually as default config.source.match (it should follow this specification).",
